incident :the_ninth_grid_hand do
  name "The Ninth Grid-Hand"
  tags :prediction, :legibility, :autonomy, :ecology

  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    In the fourth quarter of 2089 #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"}'s cabinet withheld clearance for one name on the coring team's round into the reserved band at #{ref :sanchakou, "Sanchakou"}, and the round went out with eight augers.

    The name was the ninth on the list, a grid-hand paid by the day out of the settlement's account and one of the thirteen the post's clinic does not read. His score came off #{ref :the_conversion_card, "the card"} at the roll's mean, as every unread name's does. The mean had fallen that quarter: the post's roster aggregate dropped through the weeks its own crews spent closing Compartment Twelve and moving #{ref :the_sanchakou_ring, "the settlement in front of it"} sixteen hundred metres, and every converted per-person figure fell with it. The ninth name crossed the cabinet's threshold on the arithmetic and not on anything anybody had observed about him.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :course, heading: "The Reading Nobody Could File"
    He had been to the clinic that week. #{ref :the_great_root, "The Great Root"}'s clinics state a figure to the person it was taken from and enter it in no file, so what he had was a reading he could describe and not produce, and #{ref :the_paired_month, "the conversion"} has no line for a figure arriving from outside the aggregate. He told the roll keeper, the roll keeper told the coring room, and the round went out anyway, because the card was signed and current and clearance is the cabinet's to give.

    #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"} entered nineteen cores where the grid calls for twenty and wrote the missing grid line and the reason on the same sheet. Her comparison drawer holds nineteen for that quarter and the reach's threshold of four sleeves is counted against twenty, so the quarter's count was filed with a note that it could not be compared to the three before it.

    Continuity's account, printed with the clearance, is the account it has filed since 2088: a threshold applied to a converted figure is what a converted figure is for, and an entrant cleared against no reading is an entrant cleared against nothing.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :aftermath, heading: "Nine Bodies, One Entry"
    Since the first quarter of #{year :now} CE the post enters grid-hands on the round by crew and not by name: nine bodies, one crew, one line, drawn from the settlement's account. The cabinet scores what it is given a name for, so it now scores the round and not the people on it, and it has withheld nothing since.

    The clerk who made the change entered the reason on the transport book: that the post had spent a quarter's comparison to learn that a figure describing forty-four people describes none of them, and that a crew is the smallest thing the post can put on a sheet without saying something it cannot check. #{ref :nadya_tsoi, "Nadya Tsoi"} continues to be listed on the card's reverse by name, because a marking officer must be named.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The withholding follows from a fall in the aggregate rather than from anything measured about the person, which is the ecological fallacy operating as a procedure. The correction the post reached — reporting a crew instead of nine names — is the same move a labour counter makes when it engages bodies it cannot identify, arrived at from the opposite direction: here the object is to give a forecasting model nothing individual to be wrong about."
end
